.\" man/man3/TreeSitter::Detector.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "TreeSitter::Detector" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Detector \- Guesses the language of source text that has no file name, such as a snippet.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter/detect"\fR
.sp
\fBclass TreeSitter::Detector\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Guesses the language of source text that has no file name, such as a snippet. A calibrated \fB\%RLCD::Model\fR trained
on code samples ranks the languages. Then the grammars of the most probable ones parse the text, and candidates
whose parse has errors lose probability to those that parse cleanly. Labels are grammar names for
\fB\%Language.find\fR. A detector reuses one \fB\%Parser\fR, so it is not safe to share between threads.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBMISSING_BYTES = 1\fR
Bytes of error that each node inserted by the parser (\fB\%Node#missing?\fR) counts for.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.load(path : String) : Detector\fR
Loads a detector saved with \fB\%save\fR, JSON or binary (detected from the content); raises \fB\%RLCD::FormatError\fR for a
malformed file.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(model : RLCD::Model, checked : Int32 = 3, penalty : Float64 = 1.0, threshold : Float64 = 0.5)\fR
A detector over \fImodel\fR, whose labels are grammar names.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.train(samples : Hash(String, Array(String)), *, dim : Int32 = 4096, seed : UInt64 = 42_u64, hidden : Int32 = 0, epochs : Int32 = 60, lr : Float64 = 0.01, validation : Float64 = 0.15, rng : Random = Random.new) : Detector\fR
Trains a detector on \fIsamples\fR: grammar name \[u2192] code snippets, for at least two languages with a snippet each.
Snippets hash into \fIdim\fR code features with \fIseed\fR. A linear head (or a \fIhidden\fR layer) learns with the log score
for \fIepochs\fR at rate \fIlr\fR. A temperature fitted on the \fIvalidation\fR share of each language\(aqs snippets
calibrates it. The model keeps the optimizer state, so training can resume.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef checked : Int32\fR
How many of the most probable languages get the parse check.
.TP 4
\fBdef checked=(checked : Int32)\fR
How many of the most probable languages get the parse check.
.TP 4
\fBdef detect(text : String, threshold : Float64 = @threshold) : Detection\fR
Ranks the languages for \fItext\fR: the model\(aqs probabilities, with the \fB\%checked\fR most probable reweighted by how
well their grammars parse it. Their share of the total stays the same. Languages without a loadable grammar
are not reweighted.
.TP 4
\fBdef labels : Array(String)\fR
The languages the detector knows, as grammar names.
.TP 4
\fBdef model : RLCD::Model\fR
The classifier: code featurizer, policy, labels and temperature.
.TP 4
\fBdef penalty : Float64\fR
How strongly parse errors count: a checked candidate\(aqs probability is multiplied by \fB\%exp(\-penalty \%* \%error_ratio)\fR
before the checked candidates share their probability again.
.TP 4
\fBdef penalty=(penalty : Float64)\fR
How strongly parse errors count: a checked candidate\(aqs probability is multiplied by \fB\%exp(\-penalty \%* \%error_ratio)\fR
before the checked candidates share their probability again.
.TP 4
\fBdef save(path : String, format : RLCD::Format = RLCD::Format.from_path(path), precision : RLCD::Precision = RLCD::Precision::F64) : Nil\fR
Saves the model to \fIpath\fR: JSON for a \fB\%.json\fR extension, binary otherwise, with weights stored at \fIprecision\fR
(binary only).
.TP 4
\fBdef threshold : Float64\fR
The probability \fB\%Detection#language\fR needs by default.
.TP 4
\fBdef threshold=(threshold : Float64)\fR
The probability \fB\%Detection#language\fR needs by default.
